    schema:description "Position Jung von Matt is looking for an Account Director (d/f/m) for our INDUSTRY Unit with a focus on B2B clients and complex brand environments. Do you excel at driving impactful campaigns and projects that truly make a difference? Are you an expert in steering complex projects to success, with a knack for delivering results on time and within budget? If so, as our Account Director (d/f/m), we’d love for you to bring your expertise to guide our projects forward. If you’re fluent in both German and English and thrive in a fast‑paced, dynamic environment, you’re the person we’ve been waiting for. Your tasks: Overall responsibility for large and complex B2B accounts and projects, including timing, cost, quality and feasibility Management, maintenance, further development and expansion of the clients Strategic and conceptual consulting for our clients Independent execution of campaign projects Leading, coordinating, and providing technical guidance to interdisciplinary teams Preparing and delivering presentations Budget planning and control, as well as project controlling What you score with: A degree in business administration, media, economics or communication sciences or a comparable education (e.g. apprenticeship) At least 7 years of hands-on experience in project management, ideally in an agency An extensive customer-, market- and brand understanding, for B2B clients Sound experience in campaign processes - briefing, calculation and especially production experience You like working in a team and you are a proactive, strong communicator You are familiar with the use of project management tools and agile working methods You feel confident in running meetings, presenting and corresponding and for steering meetings in the right direction You are very well organized and you easily maintain an overview What we offer: Professional growth: Access extensive training opportunities, including language courses in German and English, along with a variety of internal programs for personal development Health and wellness: Receive a subsidized Wellpass membership and support for mental health through mindfulness sessions and coaching opportunities Family and lifestyle support: Utilize our Parents Program and bike leasing options Annual leave: Enjoy 30 days of vacation to recharge and maintain your creativity Exclusive discounts: Enjoy corporate benefits with employee discounts on various services and products Engaging events: Participate in unique activities like Cinema Tuesdays and our annual ski trip, the Brettertour Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
