    schema:datePosted "2026-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Short Description INERATEC’s innovative chemical reactor technology is a key enabler of the energy transition. We build chemical plants that use greenhouse gases such as CO₂ and renewable electricity to produce synthetic fuels and sustainable products. As Engineering Manager (m/f/d), you will act as the central technical interface for the planning, execution, and operational realization of complex Power-to-X and e-fuels plants within an EPC/EPCM environment. You will lead engineering activities across disciplines and coordinate interfaces between process engineering, plant design, electrical/instrumentation engineering, automation, and permitting. #sort: 140#PES# Your tasks Overall technical responsibility for EPC plants, including engineering coordination across all disciplines Leadership of the internal engineering team and interface management with Operations, Manufacturing, Procurement, and Project Management Management of external engineering partners, EPC contractors, and specialist planners, including tendering, contract and performance management, and claims management Coordination and approval of process engineering fundamentals, including PFDs, P&IDs, balances, control concepts, and safety concepts Change management, including assessment of technical, schedule, and commercial impacts Review and approval of technical calculations, supplier documentation, and manufacturing/installation documentation Technical support for permitting and approval engineering, including coordination with authorities, inspection bodies, and external experts Your profile University degree in Process Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Plant Engineering, Environmental Engineering, or a comparable qualification Several years of professional experience as a Lead Engineer or Engineering Manager (m/f/d) in plant construction and process engineering, ideally in the chemical or petrochemical industry Experience in technically leading engineering teams within EPC/EPCM projects Independent, proactive, and responsible working style Strong assertiveness and a solution-oriented approach Very good written and spoken German and English Why us? A fast-growing and dynamic CleatTech with a clear mission Flat hierarchies and an open corporate culture Flexible working hours and the possibility to work hybrid or mobile Plenty of room for personal initiative/creative freedom as well as personal and professional development Varied and responsible tasks Company pension scheme Fitness studio cooperation Attractive health offers on the pulse of time Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
