    schema:datePosted "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Join us in our mission to transform the way people shop and eat, where impact, innovation, and growth drives everything we do. Our Brand & Experience team builds the emotional connection between Deliveroo and our customers, riders, and partners. With a deep understanding of our audience and a passion for creativity, we bring our brand to life across every touchpoint. Whether it’s a push notification, social campaign, or packaging design—we craft compelling experiences that shape perceptions, spark engagement, and make Deliveroo a loved, global brand. We're hiring a Local Lead, Creative Campaigns to join Deliveroo's Global Marketing team on a 8-month fixed-term contract, covering maternity leave from mid-late September 2026. This is a hybrid role, based in Paris. Reporting into the Director of Creative Strategy & Campaigns, you'll lead the development and delivery of global brand campaigns and activations across Deliveroo's markets, partnering closely with teams across Marketing, Product, Research, Media, Social and our in-house Creative Studio. Given the Global nature of the position, we are looking for a candidate who is bi-lingual in French and English at minimum; ideally Italian too. This role comes at an exciting point in our campaign calendar. You'll be stepping into an active programme of high-profile work, so we're looking for someone who can quickly build context, establish strong relationships and confidently take ownership of multiple projects from the outset. You'll be supported by an experienced team, but you'll be comfortable navigating ambiguity, making decisions and maintaining momentum in a fast-moving environment. This role follows our hybrid working policy, with three days per week in our Paris HQ. Given the Global nature of the team and campaigns we work on, travel to our offices in London, Milan and UAE may be an opportunity too. What you'll be doing Lead global brand campaigns Own the end-to-end development of key global campaigns - from defining creative objectives and writing briefs through to creative development, production, localisation and rollout across our markets (UK, France, Italy, Belgium and UAE). You'll work closely with Integrated Marketing, Media, Insights, PR and Social teams to ensure campaigns are creatively distinctive and commercially effective. International team leadership You will lead a team of 3, developing campaigns across different markets and with different culture, language and local market context. You will inspire across these geographical boundaries and foster an inclusive team culture. Working with your local teams, you will aspire to learn about the different customer behaviours and culture in our markets, to ensure our marketing is as effective as possible. Drive creative excellence Partner with our Creative Director, in-house Creative Studio and external creative & media agencies to develop bold, channel-appropriate creative that strengthens Deliveroo's brand. You'll champion high creative standards while balancing speed, quality and operational excellence. Transcreation for different markets is a key part of this role, so you will look for ideas that can flex for different audiences and languages. Deliver integrated production Lead complex multi-channel productions across TV, OOH, digital, social, radio and in-app experiences, ensuring campaigns are delivered on time, on budget and to a consistently high standard. Measure and improve performance Work with Marketing Effectiveness and Insights teams to evaluate campaign performance, identify learnings and translate those into actionable recommendations that continuously improve our creative output. Build capability across the business Develop creative frameworks, playbooks and best practice that help global and local teams deliver stronger campaigns more consistently. Foster close collaboration across functions and markets to ensure ideas travel well while remaining locally relevant. What we're looking for We're looking for someone who combines strategic thinking with excellent campaign delivery and thrives in a collaborative, fast-moving environment. You'll bring: 8+ years proven experience working in a similar role and delivering impactful global or multi-market campaigns with significant experience in creative strategy, development of big ideas through to an integrated plan across a brand’s ecosystem Experience in delivering TTL production (including TV, OOH, digital, social, radio) Experience managing creative agencies Bi-lingual in French and English at minimum; ideally Italian too. International team leadership experience Strong interpersonal skills to manage global and cross-departmental stakeholders and partners Attention to detail Experience communicating with senior leadership A self-starter attitude with the ability to thrive in a fast-paced, matrix environment Ability to navigate ambitious and complex projects Agency experience is a plus, but not mandatory Experience working at or with a retail/eComm/tech/FMCG company preferred Why Join Us? At Deliveroo, you’ll do work that matters, solving real-world problems in a three-sided marketplace that’s constantly evolving. We’re food lovers, problem solvers, community builders and more, brought together by a shared drive to make things better. Working here you can expect to: 🔧 Make a visible impact every day Your work directly improves experiences for customers, partners and riders. 🌱 Learn fast in an entrepreneurial environment Work close to the market with autonomy, pace and real responsibility. 🧠 Build a career, not just a role Stretch yourself, develop new skills and grow as the business evolves. 🌎 Deliver together in an inclusive culture Collaborative, values-driven teams that support how you work best. We aim to create a fair process that lets your skills shine—our interview typically includes 3-4 stages. Find more about how we hire here. Our Global Structure Deliveroo is now part of DoorDash, bringing together teams with even greater reach, scale, and ambition. Depending on your role, you may collaborate with teammates, systems, and leaders across DoorDash and Wolt. Together, we’re unlocking new possibilities as one global team. Diversity, Equity and Inclusion At Deliveroo, we know that a great workplace reflects the world around us and that true diversity and inclusion make us stronger, more creative, and better at what we do. We’re committed to fostering an environment where everyone can do their best work and feel they belong. We believe in equality of opportunity and welcome candidates from all backgrounds regardless of age, gender, ethnicity, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, socio-economic background, religion, or belief. If you have a disability or long-term health condition and need support to apply for one of our roles, or require any reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process, you’ll have the opportunity to let us know once you’ve submitted your application. We’ll share details on how to request support so we can ensure you have a fair and equitable experience. If you’re excited about making a real impact in a fast-moving marketplace and growing your career alongside ambitious, supportive teams, we’d love to hear from you! Find more English Speaking Jobs in France on Arbeitnow" ;
