    schema:description "About Working at envelio Too easy is boring! Together, we are on a mission to drive forward the energy transition. We love what we do, and we are unafraid to dive in. We believe in taking ownership of our work and in continuously growing and evolving. In short: own it, love it, grow with it. We are a humble team of coffee and maté lovers with over 20 nationalities. With our geek humor, our love for emojis and random facts is only natural. Over 200 envelians are already on board. Dive in and thrive! Your Role As a Working Student in Market Intelligence, you will support our International Expansion and Commercial teams by building and maintaining a scalable market intelligence framework. You combine a commercial and economics interest with a data-driven mindset, and you enjoy creating clarity in complex, fast-changing environments. How You Make an Impact You build out and maintain our internal market intelligence framework, including: regular scouting of market developments and trends across relevant countries deep-dives into country regulations and market drivers structured market monitoring of the industry landscape (e.g., relevant players, initiatives, partnerships, news) smart utilisation of internal knowledge (e.g., learnings from Sales, Customer Success, Product) You keep our internal databases that support the market intelligence framework up to date and continuously improve data quality (structure, completeness, consistency) You enhance the market intelligence/analytics framework by contributing toprocess automation and by incorporating additional input sources (where useful and feasible) You support the team with structured research deliverables (e.g., market snapshots, short briefs, summaries for decision-making) and maintain clear documentation Your Profile You are currently enrolled in a bachelor’s or master’s degree program (e.g., business, economics, industrial engineering, data/analytics, political science, or a comparable field) You have a strong interest in markets, regulation, and commercial strategy — and you like combining this with a data-driven mindset You work in an organised and structured way and can balance attention to detail with making pragmatic, high-level assumptions when needed You are familiar and confident in using AI tools and automation approaches to improve research and documentation workflows Communicating in English is no problem for you; German and/or additional European languages are a plus Your Benefits Flexible working mode within Germany: Hybrid, from home or in our lovely office in Cologne Option for remote work from abroad (up to three months per year from anywhere in the EU or the USA) 20 holidays + 3 corporate holidays Support for your health through sports membership cooperations Professional mental wellbeing support through our partner nilo for you and your family Flexible use of a monthly mobility budget (e.g. Jobrad, public transport) Time and resources for individual growth Regular tech & growth talks for internal knowledge sharing Regular company and team events Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Part time, Student, Working student" ;
