    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "e94cee120c3b3216e5cef4514ed8f9c77cdcee826a235db16f4cf5040fd3defc" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-09-07T07:54:08+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-09-07T07:54:08+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:reconciliationReason "no reviewed first-party candidate" ;
    kgjobs:sourceOccurrence <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/jobs/live/occurrence/arbeitnow-tech-advisory-senior-consultant-munchen-59206/1> ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "tech-advisory-senior-consultant-munchen-59206" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "YOUR TASKS As a Senior Consultant (m/f/d) in the Tech Advisory area, you will take on a key role in complex transformation projects. You will support our clients in the digital and organizational evolution of their business models and processes - from strategy development through to operational implementation. You will work at the intersection of business, technology, and change management, applying agile methodologies in a targeted and effective way. In transformation projects, you will play a central role by bringing structure, clarity, and strong execution capabilities. Your responsibilities will include a wide range of tasks: Supporting transformation initiatives: Assisting clients in the structured development and optimization of organizations, processes, and ways of working Interface management between business and IT: Gathering, structuring, and aligning business requirements while ensuring a shared understanding of project objectives (Partial) project management: Independently planning, coordinating, and delivering projects with a strong focus on sustainable results Applying agile methodologies: Using agile ways of working and taking on relevant roles (e.g. Scrum Master or Product Owner) within projects Change management: Designing and supporting transformation processes, including stakeholder management and implementation support Process analysis and optimization: Identifying improvement opportunities and developing as well as implementing efficient, digitally enabled processes Management-level communication and reporting: Conducting structured analyses and preparing content tailored to decision-makers and steering committees YOUR PROFIL We are looking for people with drive, a strong sense of responsibility, and a clear affinity for technology and transformation. What you should bring to the role: A completed degree in (Business) Informatics, Engineering, Business Administration, or a comparable field of study Several years of professional experience (at least 3–5 years) in management consulting or in transformation/digitalization projects Certification in agile project management, ideally as a Scrum Master or Product Owner, as well as hands-on experience applying agile methodologies Strong technological understanding: Ability to translate modern technologies (Cloud, Data & AI, Cybersecurity) into scalable IT architectures and digital platforms Project management expertise: Experience managing (sub-)projects, including planning, steering, and stakeholder communication Experience in transformation and change management: Ability to support organizational change in a structured way and ensure sustainable implementation Strong analytical and strategic thinking skills combined with a pragmatic, solution-oriented working style Excellent MS Office skills (especially PowerPoint and Excel), along with strong presentation and communication abilities High level of initiative, strong teamwork skills, and a customer-oriented mindset You have very good German and English language skills (minimum C1 level in both languages) YOUR BENEFITS Supportive Team Culture: Team cohesion is important to us - we support one another and foster a healthy office culture. Our event team organizes regular after-work events to encourage exchange and connection beyond the workplace. Early Ownership & Responsibility: From day one, you will take on exciting tasks with real responsibility – whether on your project or by contributing to internal initiatives. You help shape the way we work. Clear Career Development Paths: You will find an environment that supports, challenges, and advances your professional growth. We offer clearly defined career paths and a transparent competency framework for every level. Creative Work Environment: We give you the freedom and time to develop creative solutions and provide the best, most modern hardware to support you (Apple or Windows). Employee Benefits: Flexible working models, a BahnCard, JobRad, Spendit card, Wellpass, and a company pension scheme contribute to your well-being. In addition, you’ll enjoy the best coffee from our new espresso machine and a fully stocked soft drinks fridge in the office. Attractive Vacation Policy: You benefit from 30 days of paid vacation per year and the flexibility to work from home. Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Experienced, Full time, Permanent" ;
